<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">England</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">England is a country in the south of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-great-britain">Great Britain</a>. A rising maritime and commercial power from the sixteenth century, it united with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scotland">Scotland</a> in 1707 to form Great <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> and became the core of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/british-empire">British Empire</a>. It appears in the histories of many other empires, from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/third-crusade">Third Crusade</a> against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ayyubid-empire">Ayyubid Empire</a> to rivalry with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spanish-empire">Spanish Empire</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch-empire">Dutch Empire</a> and diplomacy with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/safavid-empire">Safavid Empire</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/england.jpg" alt="England" width="320" height="192" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Original: traditional Vector: Nicholas Shanks · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_England.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
